					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "HSB is an alternative for RGB.\nBoth produce colors in the end, but HSB is considered a more \"human\" approach to color.\nInstead of controlling the individual color channels you'll be controlling the hue, saturation and brightness.\n\nA big advantage of the HSB system is that it is very easy to create variations of a given color.\nThe second example demonstrates how the Linear node can be used to create a variation above and below the selected hue.\n\nNote that some video effects like Hue Rotate, InvertRGB and Greyscale can also be used on the Color type"
					}
				},
